{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":165,"timestamp":"2026-07-22T17:04:28.559765Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5b34459f-702c-4b3e-a162-d109cfd9d4b2","comment_uuid":"078dd7ad-a3be-49de-b680-10fda4958d8b","author":"xqjG","content":"THIRD MDATRON RAISE (operator-caught 2026-07-22, correcting the crosslink strict-YAML item's routing): the design.md defect ALSO goes to mdatron, and it is the more structural of the two. The crosslink side (ship valid YAML) fixes one file; the mdatron side fixes the class. RAISE 3 — SCOPING / IGNORE LIST: mdatron walks every frontmatter-bearing markdown in the tree, including files it neither owns nor should govern — chassis-deployed command files, third-party artifacts. A malformed third-party file therefore blocks the CONSUMER's commits over a document mdatron has no mandate to validate. Passes the three-question gate: in scope (which markdown mdatron validates is core Schematron-for-markdown territory), unsupported today (it walks all), generic (any consumer with third-party-deployed markdown wants it). Asks: a route-table-style ALLOWLIST (mdatron validates only what a consumer explicitly routes — Thermite's spec-routes.toml is the precedent, and the estate's own contract already carries a closed-world route table as a first-class concept) OR an IGNORE LIST as the lighter interim; plus a stated default (walk-all vs route-only) — the route-only default is the closed-world-correct one. This retires the design.md incident's whole class: with routing, an unrouted chassis command file is simply not mdatron's to refuse. The crosslink filing stays drafted (ship valid YAML regardless); the mdatron raise is the durable fix. Relay text for carriage delivered in-session alongside raises 1 and 2.","created_at":"2026-07-22T17:04:28.542609Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvb