{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":311,"timestamp":"2026-07-26T00:00:50.930446Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"358ca9e3-c16b-436b-8e2c-cad2c1ad11a3","comment_uuid":"3945217a-0e91-4da4-90e3-ebbe8fc73675","author":"xqjG","content":"LAYER 3 ENTRY (operator directive 2026-07-25: 'Enter Layer 3'; classification: phase-transition directive, scope exactly the decomposition's Layer 3 — the three renderings and the wiring script; the #665 amendment applies: the entry is named by the work, 2a-author-red-gate-tests, and the first work commit carries it). Milestone #6 created. DEPENDS ON, per the decomposition: Layer 2's phase answer and snapshot fields (signed off at 287d1ab0), Layer 1's statusline data artifacts (width budgets 16/20/24/34, wall-clock 250ms with the 7-run median rule and twice-budget ceiling, truncation mark and rule, broken-state mark, degraded next-step texts, repo-set config shape — all standing in statusline-data 0.2.0). HAND-CARRIED OBLIGATIONS AT THIS ENTRY, per the decomposition preamble, recorded now: (1) the operator-authored manual-test checklist for Layer 3 (manual-tests/layer-3.md — the operator authors the oracle; a draft proposal follows for adoption or replacement); (2) the layer's red-gate seed (proposal follows for adoption). CARRIED ITEMS FOLDED INTO THIS LAYER'S SCOPE: #740 (the broken-state answer carries the last boundary truth from git — joins the broken-state branch's composition); the position/health facets design note (recorded on #738: named blocks answer/report in the machine form, two sections in the human form, health detail is pull); the diagnostic-format alignment item (vsdd's human render grammar aligns to mdatron's exact rustc shape — the engineering-conventions disposition from the boundary sweep); #713 (the vanished user-level statusLine wiring — the wiring script this layer builds is the re-wire vehicle; the operator's settings write itself stays an operator or Layer 4 act). ARCHITECTURE NOTE, from the decomposition's criteria audit: Layers 3 and 4 map to the vsdd BINARY crate — this layer's modules land in vsdd/src/, consuming vsdd-core's Layer 1/2 behavior across the crate seam; one new core seam is owed (the last-boundary git query rides the bounded runner, which is core-internal).","created_at":"2026-07-26T00:00:50.915626Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAP9ukEU5mnz9PH+sDn+NT4qeqwUw17QKLiGzlATowBz2WpgQrWILx2eSx8Aev6u4ZtsOJJJoVNb8B/sOwvNSDAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBhpp2H081jMXpgR9gaNxGTg2ME7f1RgWcV5y81C7YejnMz0V0sz5CNPXm6lfs2jh9LPwLwyK305HGUioP2wkwg="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":312,"timestamp":"2026-07-26T00:01:18.779344Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"358ca9e3-c16b-436b-8e2c-cad2c1ad11a3","comment_uuid":"43f67bc0-1e84-402b-86ab-ac71e73a2fa2","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-2A DESIGN ACT — the crate-level module map (draft, for operator adoption). All in the vsdd binary crate per the architecture sketch: vsdd/src/status/mod.rs — the composition root and effectful shell: ONE acquisition, ONE derivation, ONE rendering per invocation; composes the broken-state outputs on all three surfaces when the state read fails; hosts the instrument seams. vsdd/src/status/segment.rs — the PURE segment renderer: (answer-or-broken, display fields, the loaded statusline data) to one line; field order repo-name/phase-answer/work-item/milestone-with-count; per-field width budgets with the (cut) mark set off by a space and the milestone name truncating before the count; worded absences from the data; the degraded marker as the kind's plain marker word; no session field; deterministic byte-for-byte; color as optional decoration only. vsdd/src/status/human.rs — the PURE human form: TWO SECTIONS per the adopted facets note — the answer (position: phase, layer, next action, composition) and the report (health: degraded kind with its full next-step text, integrity findings, substrate findings); superset of every segment field plus the session rendering (the demotion ruling); broken-state renders the rustc-shaped diagnostic with per-kind recovery, its grammar aligned to mdatron's exact rendering shape (the boundary-sweep disposition, executed here). vsdd/src/status/machine.rs — the PURE machine form: named blocks answer and report; broken-state is the structured state-unreadable signal (enumerated kind, diagnostic payload, recovery action from the vocabulary); superset-of-segment verified. vsdd/src/status/broken.rs — the shared broken-state composition, carrying #740: the last-boundary truth (the most recent boundary commit's subject from a bounded git log query — a new pub seam in vsdd-core's shell since the runner is core-internal) rendered as recovery context on the human and machine forms; absence of a boundary commit is a worded absence, never a failure. vsdd/src/status/instruments.rs — the conduct seams: the counting stdin wrapper (the statusline path reads zero bytes; the sentinel fixture backs the count), the acquisition counter, the whole-invocation wall-clock against the 250ms budget with the 7-run median and twice-budget ceiling; model-absence is the test environment's property (no credentials, no network), documented not coded. vsdd/src/status/multi.rs — the composed multi-repo display over the explicit repo-set config ({repos, per_repo_budget_ms} at the registered location): one segment line per repo, current first, per-line worded repo identity, every single-segment conduct check holding per line. templates/statusline/vsdd-statusline.sh — the wiring script (installed by Layer 4, authored here): reads the repo-set config, invokes the composed display, passes the substrate's stdin through unconsumed, aggregate cost denominated repo-count-times-per-repo-budget; ownership and drift refusal per the managed-file discipline; the non-wrapper composition instruction ships beside it per the registered conduct.","created_at":"2026-07-26T00:01:18.765976Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAI3Jca7qVmoOKtQMKvZKiXWCc+sCUU6rRg8OVrivY1kNxHMOSsIyCh4A0fuWvT9407GZRnNfK7NToypEwjtN0Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLiEZQ864dJl98r1q0cewaNwCNUg77UjhJS0BGI22kpuXV1sQWg